{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Amadeus8 AC Service → NestJS Backend API",
    "version": "3.0.0",
    "description": "All HTTP calls that the Amadeus8 C# service makes TO the NestJS backend, plus NestJS callback endpoints available for the C# service.\n\nChanges in v4.0.0:\n- Added POST /api/access-control/import/callback (NestJS import callback endpoint — not currently called by C#, polling used instead).\n- Added POST /api/access-control/import/access-levels/callback (NestJS access-level callback — not currently called by C#).\n- Noted stale BackendApiDefinitions references: GET /api/access-groups, /api/security-groups, /api/cardholders are defined but route paths do NOT exist on NestJS (actual paths are /api/access-control/*).\n\nv3.0.0 notes (retained):\n- All NestJS responses are wrapped in ApiResponseEnvelope { success, data, timestamp } via global TransformResponseInterceptor.\n- GET /api/events/amadeus now uses page + limit pagination (returns PaginatedResult). Previously used limit-only.\n- BackendApiClient unwraps envelope for GET endpoints via BackendApiEnvelope<T> (reads .data field).\n- BackendApiClient reads POST /api/sync/full response directly as SyncResultDto (outer 'success' maps to SyncResultDto.Success; inner data fields are lost — known gap).\n- Individual sync routes (/api/sync/controllers, /doors, /extensions, /access-groups, /security-groups, /cardholders) are defined in BackendApiDefinitions but NOT called by BackendApiClient. Retained for documentation.\n- BackendAmadeusEventDto.logId is int64 (long in C#).\n\nv2.0.0 notes (retained):\n- Added POST /api/sync/controllers, /doors, /extensions, /access-groups, /security-groups, /access-levels, /cardholders (7 routes).\n- Added GET /api/events/amadeus.\n- SyncResultDto includes 'succeeded' and 'failures' fields from C# SyncResultDto."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://{host}",
      "variables": {
        "host": {
          "default": "localhost:3000"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/api/sync/full": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Trigger full startup sync",
        "operationId": "syncFull",
        "description": "Called by Amadeus8 on startup (and manually). Triggers a full upsert of all controllers, doors, door IOs, extensions, extension IOs, access groups, security groups, and cardholders into the NestJS database. Response is wrapped in ApiResponseEnvelope.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EmptyRequestBody"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Sync completed (wrapped in envelope)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ApiResponseEnvelope_SyncResultDto"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Sync failed",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SyncErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
